[{"id":"dff-predict-basic","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"The <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code> lane is the clock: each column is one cycle, from one rising edge to the next. A flip-flop copies <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> at each rising clock edge and holds it in between. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>At each rising edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> takes the value <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> has at that moment and keeps it for the whole cycle. Here <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> changes on falling edges, half-way through a cycle, so each new value of <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> at the next rising edge, half a cycle later.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"dff-basic","source":"hdl/level-02/dff/dff_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"dff_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"dff_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2.5,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[5.5,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q","path":"dff_tb.q","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[6,"1"]],"samples":["1","1","0","1","0","0","1","1"]}]},"answer":"q","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"dff-predict-pulse","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is a simulation of lesson 2.1's flip-flop, in which <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> has a short pulse in cycle 1. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>A flip-flop looks at <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> only at the rising edge. The short pulse in cycle 1 starts after edge 1 and is gone before edge 2, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> never sees it and stays 0. The pulse that starts in cycle 3 is still there at edge 4, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is 1 for cycle 4.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"dff-pulse","source":"hdl/level-02/dff/dff_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":6,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"dff_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"d","path":"dff_tb.d","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1.7,"1"],[1.9,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[4.5,"0"]]},{"label":"q","path":"dff_tb.q","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"]],"samples":["1","0","0","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"q"},{"id":"dff-fill-edge","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 2.1's flip-flop, <code class=\"nobreak\">dff.sv</code>, with one word missing. Type the word that makes it copy <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> at each rising edge of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>posedge clk</code> means the rising edge of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code>, the moment it goes from 0 to 1. So <code>always_ff @(posedge clk)</code> copies <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> once at every rising edge, and <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> keeps its value in between.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-02/dff/dff.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":11,"before":["// A D flip-flop: at every rising edge of clk, q takes the value d had","// just before the edge, then holds it until the next rising edge.","module dff (","  input  logic clk,  // the clock","  input  logic d,    // data in","  output logic q     // data out: d as it was at the last rising edge",");"],"blankLine":{"left":"  always_ff @(","right":" clk) begin"},"after":["    q <= d;","  end","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// A D flip-flop: at every rising edge of clk, q takes the value d had","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// just before the edge, then holds it until the next rising edge.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"dff","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the clock","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// data in","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// data out: d as it was at the last rising edge","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]},"after":[[{"text":"    q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["posedge"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing keyword"},{"id":"dff-find-bug","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"This flip-flop should behave like lesson 2.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">dff</code>, but its testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>Lesson 2.1's flip-flop says <code>always_ff @(posedge clk)</code>: at every rising edge. This one says <code class=\"nobreak\">negedge</code>, the falling edge, when <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code> goes from 1 to 0, so <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> changes half a cycle late. The testbench checks lesson 2.1's rule, that just after each rising edge <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> equals the value <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> had at that edge, and that fails. With <code class=\"nobreak\">posedge</code> the same testbench passes.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-02/dff_bug/dff_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A D flip-flop that should copy d to q at every rising edge of clk.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// Its testbench fails: one line is wrong.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"dff_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk,  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the clock","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" d,    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// data in","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" q     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// data out: d as it was at the last rising edge","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"negedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    q ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":8,"fixLine":"always_ff @(posedge clk) begin"},{"id":"dff-report-fdre","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built lesson 2.1's <code class=\"nobreak\">dff.sv</code> for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table from its Utilization report, <code class=\"nobreak\">utilization.rpt</code>: one row for each kind of cell the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>The FDRE row says 1: Vivado built lesson 2.1's code as a single FDRE, the D flip-flop cell with a clock enable and a reset that lesson 2.1 describes (this design uses neither). The other rows are cells for the pins and the clock; their Functional Category column says IO or Clock.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/dff/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":179,"excerpt":["8. Primitives","-------------","","+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    2 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| FDRE     |    1 |        Flop & Latch |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many FDRE flip-flops does this design use?","answer":"1","numeric":true},{"id":"dff-order-edge","itemId":"d-flip-flop","role":"core","promptHtml":"Put these in the order they happen, from just before a rising edge of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code> to after it.","explanationHtml":"<p>Before the edge, <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is steady and the flip-flop is not looking at it. At the rising edge, when <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code> goes from 0 to 1, it copies <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>. After the edge it ignores <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> again, so a change on <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> has to wait for the next rising edge to reach <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>.</p>","type":"order","steps":["`clk` is 0, and `d` holds a steady value.","`clk` goes from 0 to 1: a rising edge.","`q` takes the value `d` had at that edge.","`d` changes, but `q` keeps its value until the next rising edge."],"shuffled":[3,1,0,2]}]